{"id":"CVE-2006-4483","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-08-31T21:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T19:14:47.549Z","description":"The cURL extension files (1) ext/curl/interface.c and (2) ext/curl/streams.c in PHP before 5.1.5 permit the CURLOPT_FOLLOWLOCATION option when open_basedir or safe_mode is enabled, which allows attackers to perform unauthorized actions, possibly related to the realpath cache.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://securitytracker.com/id?1016984","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1016984"},{"url":"http://www.php.net/release_5_1_5.php","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/22039","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"22039"},{"url":"http://cvs.php.net/viewcvs.cgi/php-src/ext/curl/interface.c?r1=1.62.2.14.2.6&r2=1.62.2.14.2.7","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://cvs.php.net/viewcvs.cgi/php-src/ext/curl/interface.c?view=log","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/19582","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"19582"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/492671/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20080527 rPSA-2008-0178-1 php php-mysql php-pgsql"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/30411","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"30411"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/21546","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"21546"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2006/3318","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2006-3318"},{"url":"http://cvs.php.net/viewvc.cgi/php-src/ext/curl/streams.c?r1=1.14.2.2.2.3&r2=1.14.2.2.2.4","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://wiki.rpath.com/wiki/Advisories:rPSA-2008-0178","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.php.net/ChangeLog-5.php#5.1.5","tags":