{"id":"CVE-2006-5731","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-11-06T18:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T20:04:54.522Z","description":"Directory traversal vulnerability in classes/index.php in Lithium CMS 4.04c and earlier allows remote attackers to include and execute arbitrary local files via a .. (dot dot) in the siteconf[curl] parameter, as demonstrated by a POST to news/comment.php containing PHP code, which is stored under db/comments/news/ and included by classes/index.php.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/2702","tags":["exploit","x_refsource_EXPLOIT-DB"],"name":"2702"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/22593","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"22593"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/29966","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"lithiumcms-index-file-include(29966)"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/20871","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"20871"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2006/4361","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2006-4361"}],"exploitdb":[{"edb":"2702","title":"Lithium CMS 4.04c - '/classes/index.php' Local File Inclusion","type":"webapps","platform":"php","date":"2006-11-02","verified":"1"}],"vendors":["curl"]}
